# Review: CanvasPlugin

The spec carries only QA tests and a changelog; it declares no types, ops or feature requirements,
so the review judges whether automation exercises its QA tests. The review tool lists two items,
QA-1 and QA-3, because QA-2, QA-4 and QA-5 share QA-1's fenced block and are not parsed as separate
items. Both listed tests are driven end to end by autocue recording scripts in
`plugin-canvas/autocue/`. These scripts click through every step and fail if a target element never
appears, but they assert none of the stated expectations (node counts, breadcrumb text, live frame
contents) and no CI task runs them. Both are therefore `partial`.

Of 2 items: 0 done, 0 untested, 2 partial, 0 diverged, 0 missing.

